@startuml artrie-layering
' ============================================================================
' PersistentARTrie durability stack.  Color key:
'   blue = client/API   orange = lock-free overlay (the hot layer)
'   red = WAL/durability   grey = block storage
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 260
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
title Persistent ARTrie family — lock-free **durable** overlay stack

rectangle "**Client API**\nPersistentARTrie · …Char · …U64Compact · Vocab\ninsert_with_value · upsert · sequence insert · get · iter_prefix" as Client #BBDEFB

rectangle "**Lock-free overlay**  (the live representation)\natomic root · immutable adaptive edge stores\nByteKey · CharKey · U64Key\npath compression · copy-on-write structural sharing" as Overlay #FFE0B2

rectangle "**Durability — log before publish**\n① append + fsync WAL record   ② publish via CAS\n③ commit rank / watermark where applicable\ncheckpoint lock serializes checkpoint publication" as Dur #FFCDD2

rectangle "**Checkpoint storage**\nmmap (default)  |  io_uring + O_DIRECT (feature)\nCX/dense overlay images · retained WAL replay\nu64 compact prefix-4 profile" as Store #CFD8DC

Client --> Overlay : "read / write"
Overlay --> Dur : "publish"
Dur --> Store : "persist · fault-in"
Store ..> Overlay : "reopen → rebuild overlay\n(dense image + WAL replay)"

note bottom of Dur
  **acknowledged ⟹ durable**
  a write becomes visible only AFTER its
  WAL record is fsync-durable.
  Linearization point = the winning CAS.
  For byte/char/vocab, the watermark is
  the safe checkpoint LSN under out-of-order
  lock-free commit.
  (TLA+ checked: no lost writes)
end note
@enduml
